@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`createRentalService` keeps equipment in a map and bookings per item with precomputed `startMs`/`endMs`; `parsePeriod` and `overlaps` already define validity and the half-open overlap rule used by `book`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** reuse the booking overlap rule so availability and `book` can never disagree.
+
+**Non-Goals:** prices, booking details, pagination, cancellation.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Implement inside `createRentalService`: validate with `parsePeriod`, validate `kind` when defined, then filter equipment with `!bookings.get(id)?.some(b => overlaps(b, period))`. Alternative of a separate helper module rejected as unnecessary.
+- Sort with the default code-unit string order (`.sort()`), deterministic and locale-independent.
+- Return a fresh array of ids only, so callers cannot affect service state.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [`kind: undefined` vs. invalid] → only `undefined` means any kind; `null` or other values throw.
